  "2026-10-16T04:09:47.325Z","harness:codex","Live Sentry correlation 2026-10-16: PM-CLI-3H remains unresolved with124 events, latest2026-10-15T16:48:14Z from pm-cli@2026.10.14 Windows CI. Auto Release run38842025410 and GitHub issue1483 are blocked by this fault. This output-projection defect is distinct from pm-jsm9im, whose implemented refusal rejects already-malformed persisted item inputs. The release gate must retain this blocker until the actual compaction boundary is fixed and verified."
escape_class: production_defect
body: "## Problem\n\nPM's read-output compaction can turn valid Unicode text into an invalid UTF-16 string. Both compaction paths use `value.slice(0, 240)`. If a supplementary-plane character such as 😀 begins at UTF-16 index 239, truncation retains its high surrogate and drops its low surrogate.\n\nThe TOON encoder then correctly rejects the malformed value:\n\n```\nTypeError: Cannot encode string value containing an unpaired surrogate U+D83D at index 239\n```\n\nThe JSON path succeeds, but the returned string contains a dangling `\\ud83d`. Switching encoding therefore avoids the exception without preserving a valid Unicode prefix.\n\nThis is a PM-owned output-projection defect: the synthetic input is well-formed and encodes successfully before compaction. No malformed input is needed.\n\n## Verification and version scope\n\n- Independently reproduced through the installed public `@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/core` entrypoint from **2026.10.13**, with Node **24.19.0** and its installed `@toon-format/toon@4.1.1`\n- Separately executed the two pure compaction helpers extracted from exact **2026.10.14** source (`2024387a346bb88e0590e07cb3262e03307b997b`) and exact **2026.10.15** source (`9de83bcd9f46c1966c4bdb20639f0b6067b4687b`), followed by the installed TOON 4.1.1 encoder. All four cases produce the same error from valid input\n- Both complete source files are byte-identical between those release commits and current main `8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8`\n- The published 10.14/10.15 packages were **not independently installed or run** for this finding. This is not a claim of a new 10.15 regression\n\nSource:\n- [compactStrings, read-output-budget.ts:165–179](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/9de83bcd9f46c1966c4bdb20639f0b6067b4687b/src/sdk/read-output-budget.ts#L165-L179), blob `06c34ff6b8cdfcaec72061fd7f2bf20386606007`\n- [compactContextIntentValue, context-intent-contracts.ts:571–585](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/9de83bcd9f46c1966c4bdb20639f0b6067b4687b/src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts#L571-L585), blob `5e3a185678b60b4b7f6435be469c620f9cce2526`\n\n## Minimal public-SDK reproduction\n\nRun in an isolated consumer where the package is already installed; the example only constructs in-memory results.\n\n```js\nimport assert from \"node:assert/strict\";\nimport { applyReadOutputDimensions } from \"@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/core\";\n\nconst title = \"a\".repeat(239) + \"😀\" + \"z\".repeat(5000);\nconst input = () => ({\n  items: [{ id: \"pm-synthetic-1\", title, status: \"open\" }],\n  count: 1,\n  total: 1,\n});\n\nassert.equal(title.isWellFormed(), true);\n\nassert.throws(\n  () => applyReadOutputDimensions(\n    \"list\",\n    { outputFormat: \"toon\", outputBudget: 1000 },\n    input(),\n  ),\n  {\n    name: \"TypeError\",\n    message: \"Cannot encode string value containing an unpaired surrogate U+D83D at index 239\",\n  },\n);\n\nconst json = applyReadOutputDimensions(\n  \"list\",\n  { outputFormat: \"json\", outputBudget: 1000 },\n  input(),\n);\nassert.equal(json.read_output.strings_compacted, true);\nassert.equal(json.items[0].title.isWellFormed(), false);\n\nconst unbounded = applyReadOutputDimensions(\n  \"list\",\n  { outputFormat: \"toon\", outputBudget: \"unbounded\" },\n  input(),\n);\nassert.equal(unbounded.items[0].title, title);\n```\n\nA separate installed-module check of `attachContextIntentReceipt(\"list\", { for: \"triage\", tokenBudget: 1000 }, input())` produces `recursive_budget_compaction` with the same invalid string; rendering that result as TOON throws too.\n\nControls: putting the emoji at index **238** or **240** does not split the pair in either exact-source helper. Uncompacted input and the unbounded public-SDK case preserve the full valid text.\n\n## Impact and expected behavior\n\nBounded reads containing ordinary valid emoji/other astral characters at this boundary can fail during output rendering or token estimation. JSON consumers instead receive a malformed truncated string. This evidence concerns emitted projections; it does not demonstrate persisted tracker corruption or data loss, and it does not attribute any particular production incident.\n\nBoth compaction paths should share a Unicode-safe bounded-prefix primitive. Keep the encoder's malformed-input rejection. Avoid manufacturing lone surrogates, substituting replacement characters, or weakening output-budget accounting.\n\nAcceptance coverage should include:\n- Both ordinary output-budget and context-intent compaction, including nested records/arrays\n- Valid astral characters immediately before, across, and after the cutoff, with no lone surrogate or replacement character in retained output\n- TOON and JSON parity, plus original-input immutability and unbounded-read preservation\n- The existing preserved-string exceptions and exact rendered-budget/receipt checks\n- CLI/SDK/MCP coverage of the shared boundary, while distinguishing source tests from installed-release acceptance\n\n## Ownership / duplicate check\n\nAll-status issue/PR searches for surrogate, unpaired, Unicode, emoji, 240, the error text, and the compaction helpers found no matching output-compaction defect. [PR #1279](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1279) / [pm-cimph7](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/issues/pm-cimph7.toon) concern the already-closed shell-completion Unicode boundary, not these output helpers.\n\nThis belongs under the existing SDK read-output/context-intent lineage: [pm-5t33or](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/features/pm-5t33or.toon) (open output-budget feature), [pm-hb7ug8](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/features/pm-hb7ug8.toon) and [pm-cxr0jb](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/features/pm-cxr0jb.toon) (closed foundational features, delivered through #873). The closed cursor/history issues #1371/#1411/#1325 address different contracts."
